    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The implementation is complete. Here's what I changed to satisfy the postcode specification:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property (4-digit string, `minLength`/`maxLength` 4) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` includes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) both carry it, so it's accepted on create and returned on read. It's not in `required`, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Model (`Owner.java`)** \u2014 Added a persisted `postcode` field with `@Column(name = \"postcode\")` plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name in both directions automatically.\n\n**Validation (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)** \u2014 Added `postcodeValidForCity(owner)` to the `normalizeNewOwner` path (returns `false` \u2192 400). It:\n- passes when postcode is absent (optional),\n- rejects a non-4-digit value,\n- reuses the city\u2192region mapping (`Owner.getLocality()`) and a `REGION_POSTCODES` table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) to reject out-of-range postcodes,\n- accepts any 4-digit postcode when the city has no known region.\n\n**Schema DDL** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column to all four DB schemas (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n## Test results\nAll 3 acceptance tests pass (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`), and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.\n\nOne note: malformed postcodes (wrong length) are rejected by the schema-generated `@Size` bean validation, while out-of-range-for-region postcodes are rejected by the controller check \u2014 both yield 400, so the two rejection paths are complementary.",
